// Title: Potential AMSI Bypass Using NULL Bits
// Sigma ID: 92a974db-ab84-457f-9ec0-55db83d7a825
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2023-01-04 | Modified: 2023-05-09
// ATT&CK: defense-impairment, T1685
// Description: Detects usage of special strings/null bits in order to potentially bypass AMSI functionalities
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://github.com/r00t-3xp10it/hacking-material-books/blob/43cb1e1932c16ff1f58b755bc9ab6b096046853f/obfuscation/simple_obfuscation.md#amsi-bypass-using-null-bits-satoshi
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_powershell_amsi_null_bits_bypass.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, microsoft_xdr schema)

DeviceProcessEvents
| where ProcessCommandLine contains "if(0){{{0}}}' -f $(0 -as [char]) +" or ProcessCommandLine contains "#<NULL>"
